<title>FRANCE: RUGBY UNION-PENAUD TO MISS SCOTLAND MATCH.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-PENAUD TO MISS SCOTLAND MATCH.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French flyhalf Alain Penaud will miss Saturday's Five Nations rugby union match against Scotland at Parc des Princes because of a pulled thigh muscle, a French team spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He will be replaced by Narbonne player Pierre Bondouy.</p>
<p>The French team will be announced on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
